## Why This Is Asked

Assess real-world troubleshooting, instrumentation, and change-management skills under production-like pressure. It probes how a candidate reasons about observability, bottlenecks, and safe rollbacks in a live system.

## Key Concepts

- Observability: p95/p99 latency, error rate, queue depth, throughput
- Backpressure and rate limiting: bounded queues, controlled retries
- Idempotency and safety: ensure duplicates don’t break state
- Canary and rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple rate limiter example (token bucket)
function createRateLimiter(tokensPerWindow, windowMs) {
  let tokens = tokensPerWindow; let t0 = Date.now();
  return function allow() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = now - t0;
    if (elapsed > windowMs) { t0 = now; tokens = tokensPerWindow; }
    if (tokens > 0) { tokens--; return true; }
    return false;
  };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify a rollback safety threshold for the canary?
- Which traces, metrics, and tests would you add to prevent recurrence?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to diagnose and execute a safe, low-downtime rollout when a new image introduces instability. Focuses on rollout metadata, readiness, and quick rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Kubernetes Deployments and ReplicaSets
- Rollout history and remediation
- Readiness/Liveness probes and startup checks
- Canary/blue-green deployment patterns for safety
- Rollback with kubectl rollout undo
- Latency validation under load

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js pseudo-code using Kubernetes client to check rollout and query metrics
const k8s = require('@kubernetes/client-node');
const kc = new k8s.KubeConfig();
kc.loadFromDefault();
const apps = kc.makeApiClient(k8s.AppsV1Api);
async function checkRollout(name, ns='default') {
  const r = await apps.readNamespacedDeployment(name, ns);
  console.log(r.body.status);
}
checkRollout('orders-api', 'kcsa-prod');
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you explicitly structure a canary deployment to guarantee no more than 10% traffic to the new version while monitoring SLI/SLOs?
- What metrics and alerts would you rely on to detect regressions during rollout and trigger rollback automatically?
